{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock.py","reason":"guards the fcntl import at :72-75 but not its use at :207 (_acquire_fcntl) and :254 (write_lock_is_busy); every store write reaches _acquire_once -> _acquire_fcntl at :491, so 384 of 510 Windows failures are 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'. Needs a real Windows exclusive leg (msvcrt.locking / LockFileEx), not an fcntl-is-None skip"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py","reason":"_mkdir_lock_is_stale/_reclaim_mkdir_lock consume the fcntl_held=True flag _acquire_mkdir passes at lock.py:325-362; the staleness proof rests on flock being kernel-mediated and dying with its holder, so a Windows leg needs its own written proof here or a narrowed reclamation path. _pid_alive also calls os.kill(pid, 0), which on Windows TerminateProcess-es the target instead of probing it"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py","reason":"NEW: the single kernel-mediated exclusive-leg selector every store write-lock probe routes through. POSIX leg is fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB) verbatim; Windows leg is msvcrt.locking(LK_NBLCK). Carries the Windows staleness proof and refuses (rather than silently degrading) when no leg exists"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py","reason":"_probe_fcntl at :142/:148 is a third unguarded fcntl.flock on the SAME .ticket-write.lock path (rebar doctor --locks); it must route through the same selector or `doctor --locks` raises AttributeError on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py","reason":"NEW: drives the real acquire()/write_lock_is_busy()/_probe_fcntl() with the fcntl primitive stubbed absent and a Windows-shaped primitive supplied (POSIX-host simulation), plus a windows-latest-only native test proving the real primitive's cross-process exclusivity and release-on-process-death"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"DECLARED LATE, after the close gate correctly refused: the merged commit 2e131f2071a0 changes this file and the original file_impact did not name it. Two edits, both required to make AC4's native-test evidence readable rather than inferred. (1) The sweep's proof step needed an explicit `shell: bash` — windows-latest defaults to pwsh, so a bash `if` guard never parsed (`Missing '(' after 'if'`), the step exited in 3 seconds, and pytest never ran at all: a step that reports nothing because it silently did nothing. (2) `continue-on-error: true` on that step, answering the review advisory that a failing proof step should not halt the whole sweep. Both are CI-harness changes in service of this story's own verification, not production behaviour; no src/ file is touched by them"}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1788625254345625622,"uuid":"340d27ac-60d7-4db1-bc19-b6311729daff"}